# service_shed -- generated by tools/cad/build_shells.py from tools/cad/shells/. DO NOT EDIT.
# half-buried concrete service block, 10 x 8 x 4, vehicle tunnel through the front
# 13.0 x 8.3 m footprint, 4.8 m tall. One piece per material group, all at the
# building's own origin: `tex NAME TILE` is per model file, so a wall and a roof cannot
# share one. The y on each line is the height that group was drawn at, put back: model.c
# rebases every OBJ's lowest vertex to zero, which would otherwise land the roof on the
# ground. Hand-placed extras, if any, follow at the bottom from
# tools/cad/shells/extras/service_shed.part
piece models/own/shell/service_shed_wall.obj   0 0.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.800 0.800 0.860  tex concrete_rough 0.6
piece models/own/shell/service_shed_trim.obj   0 0.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.580 0.590 0.650  tex concrete_rough 0.7
piece models/own/shell/service_shed_roof.obj   0 4.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   0.690 0.700 0.770  tex concrete_rough 0.6
piece models/own/shell/service_shed_dark.obj   0 0.000 0   1 1 1   0 0 0   1.000 1.000 1.000

# The kit's frames, seated IN the reveals the shell cuts: each piece is pushed back
# into the wall by its own architrave projection, so the moulding finishes flush with
# the plaster instead of standing on it. Generated from the same Walls calls that cut
# the holes, so a frame and its reveal cannot drift apart.
piece models/own/arch/plain_door.obj   2.700 0.000 -3.940   1.000 1.000 1.000   0.0 0.0 0.0   1.470 1.250 0.880  tex planks_weathered 2

# ---- from tools/cad/shells/extras/service_shed.part ----
# Hand-placed, not part of the fabric: the roof plant (two pipe stacks, a railing along the +x
# side, a roof box) riding the new roof deck -- top at 4.25, five centimetres above the old flat
# roof's 4.20, and the railing pulled in from x=5.2 to x=4.65 so it stands just inside the new
# parapet instead of through it. Below that, a leaning plywood sheet propped against the front
# wall and its two cleats, unchanged from the survey since the footprint didn't move.

# roof plant
